 "hypothesis": "H67-A: an axial (cos2t, sin2t) orientation head fitted within 3 px of catalogue traces, plus a tip/junction heatmap head, let a hysteresis walk follow a lineament through gaps and extend past mapped tips along the predicted strike, so that credit is recovered on the truncated ends of known structures.",
 "mechanism": "Across-strike NMS collapses a 2-3 px evidence ridge to one path; the walk continues while evidence stays above lo (hysteresis) and, past a tip, up to max_ext_px further along the predicted orientation while evidence stays above lo_ext.  Nodes are then chosen by spacing or by the calibrated marginal-DTI rule.",
 "non_fault_mimic": "Erosional escarpments, alluvial-fan margins, terrace risers, drainage lineaments and lithological contacts are linear and satisfy the same orientation and coherence tests; the tip head gates only how far a walk may extend and does not verify that the extension is a fault.",
